cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the derived results in academic work, please cite the manuscript below. Author information is to be completed before publication."
title: "Complete genome comparison identifies an excised PBSX-like phage-related element and a conserved bacteriocin-associated plasmid in near-isogenic Enterococcus lactis genomes"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived results comparing two near-isogenic Enterococcus lactis genome
  deliveries (smbu06 and smbu08): one 38,719-bp PBSX-like phage-related element present on the
  smbu06 chromosome and excised (attJ state) in the smbu08 assembly, a 128,837-bp plasmid shared
  between the two deliveries, a candidate bacteriocin cassette, and an independent Nanopore
  long-read validation of the attJ junction and of the tandem boundary of the 77,437-bp circular
  component. Long-read mappings support the attJ junction state and the unit1-to-unit2 boundary,
  but do not distinguish a tandem dimer from a monomer circle.
